  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 210 PM MDT Sat Sep 12 2026\n\nSatellite imagery shows closed low centered off PacNW coast \ntoday with shallow ridge in place over East Idaho. Combination \nof gusty winds in a few areas and still-low humidities has \nimplications for fire weather concerns today. See that \ndiscussion below. Shortwaves ejecting northeast out of southern \nOregon today expected to cross the region overnight tonight. \nTrajectory of deepest moisture shifts mainly through western \nIdaho into the panhandle overnight, with only a very small \nportion of the central mountains seeing any potential of \nprecipitation. Most of East Idaho will remain dry with this \nfeature. The main impact will be twofold: winds Sunday and \nushering cooler temperatures by Monday. Have issued a WIND \nADVISORY for the Arco/Mud Lake/Dubois region Sunday (Zones 52 \nand 67). NBM currently showing a greater than 80% probability of\nwind gusts exceeding 45 mph across the region but a less than \n40% probability of gusts exceeding 50 mph. Temperatures cool \nSunday, but the greatest drop in daytime highs arrives Monday, \nwell behind the front. Daytime highs are generally expected to \nbe in the 60s for most of the East Idaho population. \n\nFor the rest of the week, ensemble clusters have transitioned to\nkeeping Idaho under the influence of a weak trough for the first\nhalf of the week with a split flow pattern shifting inland off\nthe Pacific for the latter half of the week. The clusters are\nshowing a lot of disagreement. NBM shows precipitation across\nportions of East Idaho by Thursday. Temperatures are expected to\nrebound back to slightly above normal through the end of the\nweek.",
